 ## Queue and Tickets
 
+Implemented in this repository: `queues` and `tickets` persistence, the
+`App\Actions\IssueTicket` issuance action and the single-call guard in
+`Ticket::call()`. Selecting *which* waiting ticket to call next (priority,
+age and fairness) is still a domain proposal below and is not implemented yet.
+
+### Queue
+
+A queue belongs to exactly one entity and is where tickets are issued.
+
+- `name` — human-readable name.
+- `slug` — unique within the entity (`entity_id`, `slug`).
+- `is_active` — defaults to `true`; inactive queues reject new tickets.
+- `labels_i18n` — optional JSON map of locale → display label.
+- Internal high-water mark for the ticket display code, so deleted ticket
+  numbers are never reused.
+
+Deleting an entity (hard delete) or a queue cascades to its queues/tickets.
+
 ### Ticket
 
-Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `called_at` and `called_by` (filled when called). Attributes:
+Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `status`, `called_at` and `called_by` (filled when called), plus `updated_at`. Attributes:
 
 - Source queue — the ticket belongs to **one** queue (within the entity); does not record which totem it came from.
-- Priority (numeric, see below).
-- Issuance timestamp (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
-- Issuance channel: totem, virtual, printed copy, etc.
+- Display `code` — per-queue sequence `A001`, `A002`, ... (`A` + at least 3 zero-padded digits; grows to `A1000`). Next code = highest valid numeric code + 1, using insertion-consistent ordering (not string ordering), skipping malformed legacy codes. Deleted numbers are not reused. Unique per `(queue_id, code)`.
+- Priority (numeric integer `>= 0`, higher = more priority, default `0`). A negative priority is rejected with `InvalidArgumentException`.
+- Issuance timestamp (`issued_at`, set to `now()`), ordering "oldest first" within same priority.
+- Issuance channel (`channel`): `totem`, `virtual` (default) or `printed`.
+- Status (`status`): `waiting` (new tickets) or `called`; there is no cancelled status.
+- Call fields: `called_at` (nullable) and `called_by_user_id` (nullable FK to users).
+
+Issuance re-reads and locks the queue row inside the transaction, so a queue
+deactivated after the caller loaded it is still rejected (`InactiveQueueException`)
+and nothing is persisted. Code insertion is retried a few times on a unique
+`(queue_id, code)` collision. Calling is allowed only for members of the
+ticket's entity (others get `AuthorizationException`), may happen exactly once,
+and a non-waiting ticket throws `LogicException` without changing call data.
 
 ### Priority
 
